# Allowlist for the single layer that `apk add --no-cache tzdata` adds on top of
# the base image. The gate (scripts/guacd-image-gate, stage 2) reads this file;
# nothing is ever read from the image under test.
#
# Measured once, from a clean `scripts/build-guacd-image` build of BASE
# (native linux/amd64, no emulation). Command, run on the saved image:
#   docker save --platform linux/amd64 <image> | tar -xO <last layer blob> \
#     | tar -t   (then every path outside usr/share/zoneinfo/, with sha256sum
#     of each regular file outside the tree)
#
# Syntax (one entry per line):
#   zoneinfo <dir>            tree: regular files without setuid/setgid/exec bits,
#                             directories, and links whose name AND target are inside
#   bookkeeping <path>        the apk files one `apk add` writes; must exist only as
#                             regular, non-executable files; contents are NOT trusted
#   extra <path> <sha256>     any other tzdata file outside the tree, pinned by content
# Parent directories of the paths below are allowed only if their mode, uid and gid
# equal the base image's. Whiteouts and any other path are refused.
#
# Fail-closed rule: if a new tzdata ships a file outside the tree, the gate fails
# and names it. Re-measure with the command above and review the diff here.

zoneinfo usr/share/zoneinfo

bookkeeping lib/apk/db/installed
bookkeeping lib/apk/db/scripts.tar
bookkeeping lib/apk/db/triggers
bookkeeping etc/apk/world

# tzdata extras outside usr/share/zoneinfo/: NONE. Measured on a clean native linux/amd64
# build of the pinned BASE with tzdata 2025b-r0: the added layer holds 1243 entries under
# usr/share/zoneinfo/ and 11 others (the four bookkeeping files above and their parent
# directories: etc, etc/apk, lib, lib/apk, lib/apk/db, usr, usr/share). A build under
# emulation that leaves other paths (for example a cache directory) is correctly refused.
